# RegAnchor aesthetic (mandatory)

Full reference: [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md). Naming/legal: [BRAND.md](BRAND.md). Tokens: `css/reganchor.css`, `css/portal.css`.

## Before changing UI

1. Open `portal.html` / `css/portal.css` and match that language.
2. Do not invent a second theme (especially dark fintech or purple-gradient startup).

## Non-negotiables

- Light paper canvas, ink `#0A0E14`, hairlines `#E6EBF1`, Blurple `#533AFD` **only** for primary actions and score meters
- Inter body; IBM Plex Sans for wordmark and score numerals
- Sentence case chrome — no stamped all-caps
- Severity = typographic colour on the label, never a parent `color` that paints the whole block
- 4px controls; ledgers over decorative cards; no glow/glass/pill clusters
- Product copy = **RegAnchor**; certificates/legal issuer = **MLA Group Ltd**
- PDF templates (`report-template.html`, `certificate-template.html`) stay self-contained CSS for Puppeteer

## Reject these patterns

```html
<!-- BAD: risk colour cascades into every child -->
<div class="dom-band" style="color:${sc.c}">...</div>

<!-- BAD: full-width pink number bar -->
<div class="act-n" style="background:${ph.color}22;color:${ph.color}">1</div>
```

```html
<!-- GOOD: ink hierarchy + meter; risk only on status word -->
<div class="dom-band">
  <div class="dom-concept-name">…</div>
  <div class="dom-meter"><span style="width:39%"></span></div>
  <span class="dom-status-pill is-risk">High risk</span>
</div>
```

If layout CSS for JS-emitted classes is missing, restore layout — do not only swap CSS variables.